{% comment %}
  zs-shortlinks.liquid — QR / short-link redirects.

  The QR codes printed on packaging point at simple paths like
  zerostickgaming.com/DSE_Box. Those paths don't exist as real pages, so
  Shopify serves the 404 template.

  Why this is JavaScript and not Liquid: on a 404, Shopify rewrites the
  request internally to /404, so Liquid's request.path never sees the
  path the visitor actually typed (the page's canonical URL comes out as
  /404 — we verified this on the live store). The browser's address bar
  DOES keep the real path, so a tiny script in <head> reads it, and on a
  match sends the visitor along instantly. location.replace also keeps
  the dead 404 page out of the phone's back button.

  theme.liquid renders this on every page; on real pages the script finds
  no match and does nothing. To add a new short link later, add one line
  to the map below: '/the-path-in-lowercase': 'https://destination'.
  Case and trailing slashes don't matter to visitors — the script
  lowercases the path and strips trailing slashes before matching.

  The zs-sl2 comment is a deploy marker: it shows up in the page source
  on every page, which is how we confirm from outside that this file
  actually reached the live theme.
{% endcomment %}
<!--zs-sl2-->
<script>
  (function () {
    var map = {
      /* The two DSE packaging QR codes -> the DSE video */
      '/dse_box_label': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gRXz2YZY388',
      '/dse_box': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gRXz2YZY388'
    };
    var path = location.pathname.toLowerCase().replace(/\/+$/, '');
    if (map[path]) location.replace(map[path]);
  })();
</script>
